The MeasureResultsTest runs by comparing data in the measure_result_map.csv to the results that are calculated dynamically
by the test, through the same path QRDA reporting uses: the patient from the database, the Measure model and the PHP
eCQM engine in CqmCalculator.

XML QRDA input files come from Cypress https://cypressdemo.healthit.gov

Import the test files using the care coordination module, or from the command line (as a user other than root):

    php bin/console openemr:ccda-newpatient-import --document=/path/to/patient.xml

then you can run the tests:

    vendor/bin/phpunit -c phpunit.xml --testsuite ECQM

Each row of measure_result_map.csv is one patient (matched by pubpid, the id from the QRDA document), one measure and
one population set, with the expected population counts from Cypress. The measure must be in the measure bundle for the
eCQM Performance Period global (Admin > Config > CDR). The measurement period runs one year from effectiveDate, as in
reporting; effectiveEndDate is not used. Set skip to 1 to leave a row out.

To see what OpenEMR calculates for patients already in the database:

    php bin/console openemr:cqm-calculate --measure=CMS122v13 --by-patient
